id: pm-efkvdy
title: Allow linked tests to opt out of source-workspace injection for self-sandboxing repo-wide gates
description: "pm test always exports PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT in schema, tracker, and auto modes. Repo-wide test runners that intentionally create their own isolated PM roots therefore change file-governance and merge-receipt semantics when linked, even though the identical direct gate passes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,context-parity,linked-tests,test-safety
created_at: "2026-07-27T19:42:44.895Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T18:31:34.675Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T18:26:52.795Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T18:26:52.795Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: A documented linked-test context mode or scoped safe control can omit source-workspace injection without allowing PM_PATH or PM_GLOBAL_PATH escape; repo-wide run-tests coverage passes both directly and as a linked test; execution_context reports the opt-out explicitly
definition_of_ready: Preserve protected tracker-root isolation and add adversarial tests proving linked metadata cannot override protected paths.
parent: pm-92if
risk: medium
confidence: 85
severity: medium
environment: pm test linked runner wrapping node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage
repro_steps: "Link node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage to an item and run pm test <id> --run; validate file-governance tests scan PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT and fail, while the same command directly passes 100/100/100/100."
resolution: Implemented per-test source-workspace isolation and snapshot modes with protected tracker roots and explicit execution receipts.
expected_result: A self-sandboxing repository gate can be recorded and executed through pm without inherited source-workspace semantics.
actual_result: All supported modes inject PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT; auto resolves to schema for non-PM commands and protected env directives cannot clear it.
fixed_version: 2026.8.22
component: linked-test-runtime
regression: false
customer_impact: Agents cannot record certain authoritative whole-repository gates as passing linked evidence without changing their semantics.
